# KF Language Protection

- ALL user-facing text (headings, descriptions, taglines, body copy, testimonials, bios, FAQ answers) must come **verbatim** from karisfellowships.com or the original KF documents.
- NEVER invent, paraphrase, or reword any text. Use exact wording from the source.
- NEVER alter language in KF documents: lessons, NHG materials, toolbox docs, meditations, worksheets, facilitator guides, or question documents.
- Lesson fidelity: never change or remove any wording in a lesson, and reproduce the source's formatting exactly (indentation, spacing, question/step numbering, centered single-spaced hymns). Only ADD formatting to match the source — never edit or drop content.
- Images/photos: never add, replace, or swap any image without explicit approval. Images are reused across pages (e.g. nhg-book.jpg is the real Neurosis and Human Growth cover, used on both register and NHG Start Here), so changing one file changes every usage. No stock/Unsplash swaps. Propose new imagery and get approval first; prefer restoring the original from git.
- If a label is needed that doesn't exist on the site, use the simplest functional word (e.g., "Open," "Download," "Back") and flag it for user review.
- When unsure, ask the user. Do not guess.
- Consult `~/.cursor/skills/karis-language/website-text.md` for the full reference text library.
